// @check
// @error operator '+' is not defined for i32 and string
// CONTRACT (must-error): `add`'s params are inference holes, and a `+` on a hole operand DEFERS its
// form to the call site (a hole is permissively assignable to string AND numeric, so the eager
// in-body check would have to guess). The call site re-validates the deferred binary-op constraint
// under the SUBSTITUTED argument types: `add(1, "x")` resolves it to `i32 + string`, which the
// emitter cannot lower, so it is a clean type error rather than a silent garbage result. The same
// one rule rejects `s + "!"` over a number and accepts every valid monomorphic shape (i32+i32,
// string+string, f64+f64) — `functions/operator-capability-poly.vl` pins the accepting half.
//
// So inference costs nothing in safety: the annotated spelling
// (`arith-annotated-mismatch.vl`) and this un-annotated one reject the same program.
function add(a, b) a + b

print(add(1, "x")) // REJECTED: i32 + string is not addable
